The vendored environment was adapted locally to use the Gymnasium reset/step
API and per-instance random number generators for reproducible rollouts.

The multivariate-normal CDF in `_adverse_event_probability` is evaluated with a
fixed quasi-Monte Carlo seed. Upstream it used the global NumPy random state,
so the expected rewards used by the SMART, Standard-of-Care, and Oracle
reference policies varied slightly between processes. Environment dynamics are
unchanged: sampled adverse events do not use this function.
